// bench_gmconsole.templ — the GM world-state CONSOLE, rehoused onto the Bench
// (C-CALV4-GM-CONSOLE). Producer + the two floors: bench_gmconsole.go.
//
// ── THE SEAT ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// A PERSISTENT GM-GATED TAB, mounted ONCE as a sibling of [data-bench-surface]
// inside .cal-bench — the same seat dayCardScaffold takes, and for the same
// three reasons (bench.templ:104 already writes them down): one per page, not
// one per Block; OUTSIDE every .cal-block-host, because `.cal-block-host .block`
// carries `overflow: hidden` and clips anything positioned inside it; and INSIDE
// .cal-bench, because every rule this surface needs is scoped `.cal-bench …` and
// a mount outside it would need a second stylesheet.
//
// IT IS NOT A FIFTH BENCH SECTION, and that is a ruling this file follows rather
// than makes. `bench_section_prefs` stores a CLOSED SET and resolveBenchSections
// defaults every key CLOSED at every width ([BR2-4] SIGNED); a <details> in the
// page flow REFLOWS, and the Weather sheet is 49 tiles — opening it would shove
// both Blocks down the page mid-session; and the SKY HEADER, the surface closest
// in kind to this one, already refused to be a fifth key by name one slice ago
// ([SKY-10]: "The header is NOT a fifth Bench section: it takes no row in the
// section store, no toggle route and no migration"). Making the console a fifth
// key one slice later would fork that ruling rather than follow it.
//
// ── WHY `position: fixed` AND NOT THE TOP LAYER ──────────────────────────────
//
// The theater's `<dialog>.showModal()` is wrong here for a reason that is about
// what the console IS: showModal makes everything behind it INERT, and this
// tool's whole job is to change the world while the GM keeps looking at the
// calendar underneath it.
//
// `popover="manual"` would avoid the inertness, and the day card on this very
// page uses it — but the top layer buys nothing here that `position: fixed`
// does not already have. The day card's own sheet documents `position: fixed`
// as the working mechanism where [popover] is unsupported
// (calendar-daycard.css:44-62), `.cal-daycard-drag` is a page-level
// `position: fixed; z-index: 40` overlay mounted from this exact region, and
// nothing between this element and the viewport establishes a containing block
// (`.cal-bench` is `display: block` with no transform/filter/contain, and
// `<main>`'s `overflow-y-auto` does not clip a fixed descendant). What the top
// layer WOULD buy is paint above every modal in the product for a control that
// is a persistent tab, not a modal — which is worse, not better. Promotion also
// costs a `showPopover()/hidePopover()` branch in gm_panel.js, a driver shared
// with the V2 console where the card is not a popover and the call would throw.
//
// ── MOTION: NONE, AND THAT IS WHY THERE IS NO SIGNATURE ──────────────────────
//
// The V2 console's chrome transitions (slide, hover lift, the mutation fade)
// live in the plugin's own gm_panel.css, which the Bench does not load. Its
// rules here are in static/css/calendar-bench.css §GM CONSOLE and declare NO
// transition, NO animation and NO @keyframes.
//
// THAT IS A DECISION, not an omission. calendar-bench.css's motion is a signed
// REGISTER ([BR2-2], decisions/2026-07-29-motion-disclosure-register.md) whose
// only enforcement is TestBenchCSS_NoMotionAtAll — and adding a third carve-out
// to it is an operator signature, not a dev call, by that guard's own words.
// Shipping the console's chrome in a NEW sheet would have kept the guard green
// while defeating it — the laundering [DC-6] refuses by name — so the rules land
// inside the guarded sheet, motion-free, and the guard covers them for free. The
// mutation fade in particular has nothing to reveal here: [SKY-13] refused the
// sky engine on the Bench, so there is no living sky to watch through the card.
//
// ── AUTHORITY ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Rendered ONLY for `data.GMConsole.Live` (cc.CanControlWorldState() — Owner or
// co-DM — AND a primary calendar). A player, a Scribe and a logged-out visitor
// receive NO MARKUP AT ALL: no control, no route string, no CSRF token, no
// disabled ghost. Permission is absence.

package calendar

import "fmt"

// benchGMConsoleView renders the console, or nothing.
//
// THE MARKUP IS THE V2 CONSOLE'S, DELIBERATELY UNCHANGED WHERE IT CAN BE. Every
// `data-gm-*` handle below is the one `gm_panel.js` already binds, because the
// driver is the SAME FILE on both surfaces — one behaviour, one state machine,
// one set of payloads, and no second copy to drift. The three departures are
// named where they occur: the mount's own attributes (below), the Owner floor on
// the Time sheet, and the absent Pause button.
templ benchGMConsoleView(c BenchGMConsole) {
	if c.Live {
		// THE MOUNT CARRIES ITS OWN ENDPOINT AND TOKEN (data-gm-url /
		// data-gm-csrf), AND THAT IS THE WHOLE REASON THIS SURFACE IS NOT
		// SILENTLY DEAD.
		//
		// gm_panel.js used to read campaignID / calendarID / CSRF off
		// `[data-cal-v2-root]` and RETURN EARLY when it was absent — an
		// attribute that exists only on calendar_v2.templ. Mounted on the Bench
		// unchanged, the console would have rendered, looked perfect, and done
		// nothing at all. The shipped fix for exactly this shape is
		// calendar_daycard.js's date-verb row, which reads `data-verb-url` /
		// `data-verb-csrf` off its own mount (bench.templ's
		// [data-bench-date-verbs]); this follows it.
		//
		// data-gm-standalone = "there is no sky engine on this page", and it is
		// ONE attribute because it is one fact with two consequences.
		// window.__calSetWorldState / __calWorldState / __calTimeControl all
		// come from static/js/cal-almanac.js, which the Bench does not load —
		// [SKY-13] refused the engine here BY ARGUMENT, and reversing that is an
		// operator signature rather than a side effect of a rehousing. So (1)
		// nothing hands this console an opening seed and it must GET one itself
		// on first open; and (2) a date move changes markup this page rendered
		// SERVER-SIDE — the Block's nameplate, its sky clock and gradient, the
		// today ring — which no seed can repaint, so the honest answer is to
		// re-read the page. That is the same call calendar_daycard.js's date
		// verbs already made and wrote down.
		<section
			class="gm-console"
			data-gm-panel
			data-gm-collapsed="true"
			data-gm-sheet=""
			data-gm-url={ c.URL }
			data-gm-csrf={ c.CSRF }
			data-gm-standalone
			aria-label="GM world-state console"
		>
			// TAB — the only thing visible when collapsed, which is how this
			// console renders on every page load. It is a tool you reach for and
			// put down, not a section you read.
			<button type="button" class="gm-console__pill" data-gm-panel-open aria-label="Open GM world-state console" title="GM world-state console">
				<i class="fa-solid fa-wand-sparkles" aria-hidden="true"></i>
				<span>GM</span>
				<i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-up gm-console__pill-caret" aria-hidden="true"></i>
			</button>
			// CARD — the pull-out. Column-reverse, so the control BAR stays
			// pinned at the bottom (always reachable) while the active sheet
			// unfolds ABOVE it. Absolutely positioned inside the fixed console
			// box: opening it causes ZERO REFLOW of the page beneath, which is
			// the property that makes it usable while the GM is watching the
			// table rather than the screen.
			<div class="gm-console__card" data-gm-panel-card>
				<div class="gm-console__strip">
					<button
						type="button"
						class="gm-console__collapse"
						data-gm-panel-toggle
						aria-expanded="true"
						aria-label="Close GM console"
					>
						<i class="fa-solid fa-xmark" aria-hidden="true"></i>
					</button>
					<span class="gm-console__title" title="GM Console">
						<i class="fa-solid fa-wand-sparkles" aria-hidden="true"></i>
					</span>
					// The clock is SERVER-RENDERED from the calendar's own
					// current time so it is right on first paint, before any
					// seed has been fetched. The driver repaints it from every
					// seed thereafter.
					<span class="gm-console__clock" data-gm-clock>{ c.Clock }</span>
					<span class="gm-console__divider" aria-hidden="true"></span>
					// THE FIVE STEP VERBS, on the CanControlWorldState floor —
					// the same predicate BenchDateVerbs.CanStep reads, and the
					// same one the route gates on. They send
					// {advance:{days,hours,minutes}}; every rollover is the
					// server's (advanceClock + validateAdvanceMagnitude).
					<div class="gm-console__verbs" role="group" aria-label="Advance time">
						<button type="button" class="gm-console__verb" data-gm-advance data-gm-minutes="10">+10m</button>
						<button type="button" class="gm-console__verb" data-gm-advance data-gm-hours="1">+1h</button>
						<button type="button" class="gm-console__verb" data-gm-advance data-gm-hours="8" title="Long rest (8h)">Rest</button>
						<button type="button" class="gm-console__verb" data-gm-advance data-gm-days="1">+1d</button>
						<button type="button" class="gm-console__verb" data-gm-advance data-gm-hours="-1" title="Step back one hour">−1h</button>
					</div>
					<span class="gm-console__divider" aria-hidden="true"></span>
					<div class="gm-console__sections" role="group" aria-label="Console sections">
						// The Time BUTTON is gated with the Time SHEET, not
						// beside it: a section button that opens an empty sheet
						// is a control that renders and does nothing.
						if c.CanSetAbsolute {
							<button type="button" class="gm-console__section" data-gm-sheet-open="time" aria-expanded="false">Time</button>
						}
						<button type="button" class="gm-console__section" data-gm-sheet-open="weather" aria-expanded="false">Weather</button>
						<button type="button" class="gm-console__section" data-gm-sheet-open="events" aria-expanded="false">Events</button>
						<button type="button" class="gm-console__section" data-gm-sheet-open="mood" aria-expanded="false">Mood</button>
					</div>
					<span class="gm-console__divider" aria-hidden="true"></span>
					// PAUSE IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT, and it is the one control
					// this rehousing did not carry. It is the console's only
					// CLIENT-ONLY verb: it calls window.__calTimeControl /
					// window.CalParticleEngine, both of which are the sky
					// engine's, and the engine is not on this page by [SKY-13]'s
					// signed refusal. Rendered here it would be a button that
					// looks live, presses, flips its own aria-pressed and
					// freezes nothing — which is worse than its absence. There
					// is no atmosphere to pause on a surface with no atmosphere.
					<button type="button" class="gm-console__iconbtn" data-gm-reset title="Reset sky — clear weather, world-events and mood">
						<i class="fa-solid fa-broom" aria-hidden="true"></i>
					</button>
				</div>
				// ---- TIME sheet — OWNER ONLY (see bench_gmconsole.go's header
				// for why this floor and not the V2 console's) ----
				if c.CanSetAbsolute {
					<div class="gm-console__sheet" data-gm-sheet-panel="time" hidden>
						<div class="gm-console__sheet-head">
							<span class="gm-console__sheet-title">Set time &amp; date</span>
							<button type="button" class="gm-console__iconbtn" data-gm-sheet-close aria-label="Close">
								<i class="fa-solid fa-xmark" aria-hidden="true"></i>
							</button>
						</div>
						<div class="gm-console__sheet-body gm-console__sheet-body--rows">
							<div class="gm-console__row">
								<span class="gm-console__lbl gm-console__lbl--inline">Time</span>
								<input
									type="number"
									min="0"
									class="gm-console__input gm-console__input--num"
									data-gm-time-hour
									value={ fmt.Sprintf("%d", c.Hour) }
									aria-label="Hour"
								/>
								<span class="gm-console__sep">:</span>
								<input
									type="number"
									min="0"
									class="gm-console__input gm-console__input--num"
									data-gm-time-minute
									value={ fmt.Sprintf("%d", c.Minute) }
									aria-label="Minute"
								/>
								<button type="button" class="gm-console__btn" data-gm-set-time>Set</button>
							</div>
							<div class="gm-console__row">
								<span class="gm-console__lbl gm-console__lbl--inline">Date</span>
								<input
									type="number"
									min="1"
									class="gm-console__input gm-console__input--num"
									data-gm-date-day
									value={ fmt.Sprintf("%d", c.Day) }
									aria-label="Day"
								/>
								<select class="gm-console__input" data-gm-date-month aria-label="Month">
									for i, name := range c.Months {
										if i == c.Month-1 {
											<option value={ fmt.Sprintf("%d", i+1) } selected>{ name }</option>
										} else {
											<option value={ fmt.Sprintf("%d", i+1) }>{ name }</option>
										}
									}
								</select>
								<input
									type="number"
									class="gm-console__input gm-console__input--num"
									data-gm-date-year
									value={ fmt.Sprintf("%d", c.Year) }
									aria-label="Year"
								/>
								<button type="button" class="gm-console__btn" data-gm-set-date>Set date</button>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>
				}
				// ---- WEATHER sheet — the full catalog, one tap sets the
				// condition on the CURRENT date. The tiles' active ring is
				// filled in by the driver from the seed it pulls on first open;
				// the producer carries no world state (see bench_gmconsole.go).
				<div class="gm-console__sheet" data-gm-sheet-panel="weather" hidden>
					<div class="gm-console__sheet-head">
						<span class="gm-console__sheet-title">Weather</span>
						<input
							type="search"
							class="gm-console__input gm-console__search"
							data-gm-weather-search
							placeholder="Filter conditions…"
							aria-label="Filter weather conditions"
						/>
						<button type="button" class="gm-console__iconbtn" data-gm-sheet-close aria-label="Close">
							<i class="fa-solid fa-xmark" aria-hidden="true"></i>
						</button>
					</div>
					<div class="gm-console__sheet-body">
						<div class="gm-console__catalog" data-gm-weather-catalog>
							for _, cat := range gmWeatherCategories() {
								<div class="gm-console__cat" data-gm-cat={ cat }>{ cat }</div>
								for _, w := range gmWeatherTypes() {
									if w.Category == cat {
										<button
											type="button"
											class="gm-console__tile"
											data-gm-weather-tile
											data-gm-id={ w.ID }
											data-gm-label={ w.Label }
											data-gm-active="false"
											title={ "Set weather: " + w.Label }
										>
											<span class="gm-console__tile-glyph" aria-hidden="true">{ w.Glyph }</span>
											<span class="gm-console__tile-label">{ w.Label }</span>
										</button>
									}
								}
							}
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>
				// ---- EVENTS sheet — trigger, per-event clear, clear-all ----
				<div class="gm-console__sheet" data-gm-sheet-panel="events" hidden>
					<div class="gm-console__sheet-head">
						<span class="gm-console__sheet-title">World-events</span>
						// The active chips (and their per-event × clears) are
						// BUILT BY THE DRIVER from the seed, never server-rendered
						// here: the Bench producer carries no world state, and a
						// second source for the same list is how two surfaces
						// start disagreeing about which meteor is still falling.
						<div class="gm-console__active" data-gm-active-events></div>
						<button type="button" class="gm-console__link" data-gm-events-clear>Clear all</button>
						<input
							type="search"
							class="gm-console__input gm-console__search"
							data-gm-event-search
							placeholder="Filter events…"
							aria-label="Filter world-events"
						/>
						// THE SECOND GATE, and it is a different question from
						// the first. PutWorldState re-checks cc.CanAuthorDmOnly()
						// server-side before it stores storageVisibilityDMOnly,
						// so this absence is defence in depth rather than the
						// boundary — but a viewer who cannot author a hidden
						// event must not be offered a switch the server will
						// silently ignore.
						if c.CanAuthorDmOnly {
							<label class="gm-console__check" title="Hidden from players">
								<input type="checkbox" data-gm-event-dmonly/>
								<span><i class="fa-solid fa-user-secret" aria-hidden="true"></i> DM only</span>
							</label>
						}
						<button type="button" class="gm-console__iconbtn" data-gm-sheet-close aria-label="Close">
							<i class="fa-solid fa-xmark" aria-hidden="true"></i>
						</button>
					</div>
					<div class="gm-console__sheet-body">
						<div class="gm-console__catalog" data-gm-event-catalog>
							for _, cat := range gmCelestialCategories() {
								<div class="gm-console__cat" data-gm-cat={ cat }>{ cat }</div>
								for _, ev := range gmCelestialTypes() {
									if ev.Category == cat {
										<button
											type="button"
											class="gm-console__tile"
											data-gm-event-tile
											data-gm-id={ ev.ID }
											data-gm-label={ ev.Label }
											title={ "Trigger: " + ev.Label }
										>
											<span class="gm-console__tile-glyph" aria-hidden="true">{ ev.Glyph }</span>
											<span class="gm-console__tile-label">{ ev.Label }</span>
										</button>
									}
								}
							}
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>
				// ---- MOOD sheet ----
				<div class="gm-console__sheet" data-gm-sheet-panel="mood" hidden>
					<div class="gm-console__sheet-head">
						<span class="gm-console__sheet-title">Mood tint</span>
						<button type="button" class="gm-console__link" data-gm-mood-clear>Clear</button>
						<button type="button" class="gm-console__iconbtn" data-gm-sheet-close aria-label="Close">
							<i class="fa-solid fa-xmark" aria-hidden="true"></i>
						</button>
					</div>
					<div class="gm-console__sheet-body gm-console__sheet-body--rows">
						<div class="gm-console__swatches">
							for _, p := range gmMoodPresets() {
								<button
									type="button"
									class="gm-console__swatch"
									data-gm-mood
									data-gm-mood-color={ p.Color }
									data-gm-mood-intensity={ fmt.Sprintf("%.2f", p.Intensity) }
									style={ "background:" + p.Color }
									title={ p.Label }
									aria-label={ "Mood: " + p.Label }
								></button>
							}
						</div>
						<div class="gm-console__row">
							<label class="gm-console__custom">
								<span class="gm-console__hint">Custom</span>
								<input type="color" value="#c83232" data-gm-mood-custom aria-label="Custom mood color"/>
							</label>
							<label class="gm-console__intensity">
								<span class="gm-console__hint">Intensity</span>
								<input type="range" min="5" max="80" value="40" data-gm-mood-intensity-slider aria-label="Mood intensity"/>
							</label>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>
	}
}
